        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(proxy-capture): wrap deletePathBasedSessions in transaction",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe two DELETE statements in `deletePathBasedSessions` were executed as separate auto-commit operations. If the process crashed between the `capture_events` DELETE and the `capture_sessions` DELETE, the two tables would become inconsistent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWrap the entire read-counts + delete operations in `runSqliteImmediateTransactionSync`, matching the sibling `deleteSessions()` method.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible change. Prevents data inconsistency on crash during proxy capture session cleanup.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Uses the same `runSqliteImmediateTransactionSync` helper already used at lines 336 and 608 of the same file",
